[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
LiveKit Ingress has been installed as %%PREFIX%%/bin/livekit-ingress.

1. Edit %%ETCDIR%%/ingress.yaml: set api_key, api_secret and ws_url
   of your LiveKit server, and the Redis address.

   Redis is required: Ingress and livekit-server exchange requests and
   session state through it, so both must use the same Redis. It can run
   on another host and is not installed as a dependency; install
   databases/redis (or valkey) if you want it on this machine.

2. Let livekit-server create ingress sessions by adding to its config:

   ingress:
     rtmp_base_url: rtmp://<this host>:1935/x
     whip_base_url: http://<this host>:8080/w

3. Enable and start the service:

   sysrc livekit_ingress_enable=YES
   service livekit_ingress start

The service runs as %%LIVEKIT_INGRESS_USER%% and logs to
/var/log/livekit-ingress/livekit-ingress.log. It listens on TCP 1935 (RTMP)
and 8080 (WHIP) and uses UDP 7885 for WHIP media by default; port 9090
(http_relay_port) is used on localhost only.

For busy WHIP setups LiveKit suggests a UDP receive buffer of 5 MB. On
FreeBSD the default comes from the net.inet.udp.recvspace sysctl, capped
by kern.ipc.maxsockbuf; Ingress warns at startup when it is smaller.

By default "service livekit_ingress stop" ends all active sessions at once.
Set livekit_ingress_sig_stop=TERM to let them finish first instead.
EOM
}
]
